senses
  entry
    definition "something (manuscripts or architectural plans and models or estimates or works of art of all genres etc.) submitted for the judgment of others (as in a competition)"
    examples ("several of his submissions were rejected by publishers" "what was the date of submission of your proposal?")
    id oewn-07182229-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (entry)
  entry
    definition "the act of submitting; usually surrendering power to another"
    id oewn-01169416-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (compliance)
  entry
    definition "the condition of having submitted to control by someone or something else"
    examples ("the union was brought into submission" "his submission to the will of God")
    id oewn-14603635-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "the feeling of patient, submissive humbleness"
    id oewn-07524564-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (meekness)
  entry
    definition "a legal document summarizing an agreement between parties in a dispute to abide by the decision of an arbiter"
    id oewn-06784895-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "an agreement between parties in a dispute to abide by the decision of an arbiter"
    id oewn-06784758-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "(law) a contention presented by a lawyer to a judge or jury as part of the case they are arguing"
